1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,000
Gale crater, Mars. Every spacewalk has one question:

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:08,000
when do I have to turn back?

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Pick targets on real NASA terrain. Return in 24 minutes.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Rehearse the walk: time, oxygen and energy, minute by minute.

5
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Oxygen down 40%? It finds the point of no return
and swaps in a closer target.

6
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:24,000
No GPS on Mars: beacons guide the way back.

7
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Same tool, second site: Spirit's Columbia Hills.

8
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:30,000
MARS::404 — know when to turn back.
